module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_serializer_drops_admitted_children_from_a_malformed_body

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { FoundAtAmbiguous, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

// Consumer: directory-derived recurring_failure_mode.roster, projected by
// gunbc.design_ledgers.expected_design_failure_modes_md through docs_projection_gate.
data a_serializer_drops_admitted_children_from_a_malformed_body: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_serializer_drops_admitted_children_from_a_malformed_body" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: FoundAtAmbiguous },

  receipts: [
    "2026-10-29: instrument-dispatch generation refused gunbc.repo.repo_self_build default_from because both if/else bodies were bare assignments. The existing serializer correctly rejected them. Wrap the bodies with bash_build_stmt_list_from_nodes; test.claim.repo_self_build_environment_witness executes the real preamble producer and refuses the old construction.",
    "INVALID STATE: a construction that accepts a body of unestablished shape reaches a serializer that walks only some of that body's positional children, so admitted siblings vanish from the emitted program with no refusal. HARM: silent wrongness (DESIGN section 5) -- the emit is plausible partial output, not a located diagnostic, and a later consumer runs a different program than the one authored.",

    "OCCURRENCE, 2026-10-11, srv1 workspace bring-up findings ledger F37 (bash subshell drops the right operand), ledger v3 numbering, operator review of source pinned to main at acc218340ed6e24a9ad06c550a5494307d0320bb (a source review that did not rerun srv1). bash_build_subshell accepts any Node body. The shared bash_fold_flatten_stmt_list (v2.workflow.bash_command_fold_serialize) reads positional children 0 and 1 only, so an or_else node passed as the body keeps left and drops right, with no refusal arm (v2.extdeps.languages.bash_build). Two insufficient boundaries: the body carrier does not establish grammar membership, and the serializer turns an unestablished shape into plausible partial output. The incident's caller fix (bash_build_subshell_from_stmts) leaves the shared reader able to drop behavior through other consumers. Durable repair: establish shape at construction, preserve every admitted child, refuse malformed input. No new Bash representation. Roadmap leaf cc-structural-carriers.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: this is not a missing flatten of a well-formed cons list -- a two-child cons is the shape the walker implements. It is not a target-language defect: the same Node is admitted at construction. The class is the pair: an untyped body formal plus a walker that silently truncates. RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder -- silent drop. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- malformed bodies are authorable and the admitted-child set is decidable from the Node tree. NEXT TRIGGER: flatten (or serialize) refuses a body whose children are not the modeled statement-list encoding, and a discriminating red keeps an or_else (or other extra child) from disappearing into a green emit.",

    "OCCURRENCE, 2026-10-20, srv1 lab deploy: the object-source Decide step (gunbc.live_deploy.emit apply_object_source_pwd_config_classify) passed a bare if node as the else body where the grammar's else body is a statement list. Main's flatten read children 0 and 1 of that node (the condition and the then body) and dropped the else branch, so the emitted Decide step was plausible shell that no longer contained the unreadable-config refusal; the lab strict fold refused it and the constant marker hid the reason. Repair at the serializer: bash_fold_flatten_stmt_list refuses an over-arity list with bash_fold_serialize_stmt_list_shape_refused and the marker names the reasons (gunbc.shell_command_text shell_command_text_refused_with_cause); the intent wraps its else body in bash_build_stmt_list_from_nodes. Claims: test.claim.live_deploy.apply_no_refused_marker_witness. The bash apply emitter that built this step, apply_object_source_pwd_config_classify included, was later deleted with the typed apply cutover (gunbc#14660), and the witness's three emission claims with it; its two serializer claims remain the regression controls.",

    "OCCURRENCE, 2026-10-28, main after #15235 (486127ca2c87): the seed-build preamble's parameter defaults (gunbc.repo.repo_self_build default_from) were rewritten from a $\{VAR:-fallback} word the bash grammar cannot spell into the grammar's own if/else, and each arm was passed as a BARE STATEMENT where the body formal is a statement-list node -- the same shape as the 2026-10-20 occurrence, a third producer, eight days after the fold began refusing it. This time the refusal was loud rather than silent: the fold substitutes gunbc.shell_command_text's poison marker, so the emitted step is not plausible-but-short but a step that fails, and the artifact cannot be regenerated at all. Seven committed workflow artifacts that embed the preamble (fleet-converge, heal, heal-publish, witnesses, drift-watch, instrument-dispatch, branch-run-grant-broker) went stale together, and every PR since that needed one has hand-taken only its own hunks of the regenerated file -- #15383's commit message names the refusal as the reason. The boundary that failed is neither the serializer, which refused correctly and located its reason, nor the body carrier, which admits any Node exactly as this row says: it is that NO CLAIM READ THE PRODUCER'S OUTPUT, so a producer whose emission is refused reached main and sat for three days while the artifacts it owns drifted. Repair at the producer and at the missing shape-establishing constructor: v2.extdeps.languages.bash_build gains bash_build_if_else_from_stmts, the twin bash_build_if_from_stmts never had, and default_from builds both arms through it. Claim: test.claim.seed_build_preamble_no_marker_witness, which reads the preamble -- the previously unwatched boundary. The second half of this occurrence, that the drift was silent for three days, is gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_authored_gate_reached_by_no_execution_route.",
    "OCCURRENCE, 2026-10-29 to 2026-11-01, the hosted build steps of .github/workflows/fleet-converge.yml (gunbc#15578): two defects stacked over the same boundary, neither of them the serializer's. (a) test.claim.host.fleet_keypair_mint_witness's equality claim (where_the_fold_can_render_the_committed_body_is_the_builders_run_itself) carried an escape branch, added in 8bbf41599c4a, that returned TRUE when the model rendered the fold's refusal poison -- a refused emission was a green claim, and the claim that exists to compare the route against the committed artifact could not see a family-wide refusal anyway, because a regen installs the refused step on BOTH sides of the comparison. (b) the module's own body reader (collect_body) ended the YAML block scalar at its first BLANK line, so every claim in that module compared only the 14-line seed preamble: the build commands, which begin after a blank, were invisible to all of them. Repairs: the escape branch is deleted (plain model == committed); an empty line belongs to the block scalar, which ends at the first non-empty line below the body indent; and a new control, refusal_poison_never_reaches_a_build_step_body, reads the marker out of what the route PRODUCES and out of what the committed artifact CARRIES, with two non-vacuity legs (the preamble's own first line must be present on both model sides, so an empty render cannot pass by saying nothing). EXECUTED, not transcribed: clean tree, both controls true; with the fold's poison sentence inserted into the mint step's body at the body's own 10-space indent, the marker control goes false and the equality control goes false; a FIRST SPECIMEN at 6-space indent -- outside the block the reader collects -- printed true, which is the claim being correct about a specimen that tested nothing, recorded because it is the difference between a control that bites and one that only looks like it does. Interpreter: /cargo-target/release/gunbc version 21cfa7b12b4dcf8dac1cb06c3d424a72fbded18f-dirty, sha256 db4d65fcc9db9a91af78cc15e423511d1a6d20587de7bfc11c6d73fd733c1cb0, built 2026-11-01T06:14:07Z, arm64 session container. The needle is DERIVED, not re-typed: gunbc.shell_command_text ::shell_command_text_refusal_marker takes the token as the first word of shell_command_text_refused_poison, and the three claims that had hand-spelled the token (test.claim.live_deploy.apply_no_refused_marker_witness, test.claim.seed_build_preamble_no_marker_witness, test.claim.compiler_gate_emit_build_lane_witness) take it from there and fail closed when it cannot be derived; the removed spellings are byte-identical to the derived token, so no verdict changes. The rung ABOVE this one -- the seams that SUBSTITUTE the marker return a plain String, so a refusal is indistinguishable from a command to everything downstream and a refused body can be installed as if it were a script -- is declared on the carrier beside shell_command_text_refused_poison, with its seam list.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.bash_command_fold_serialize", decl_name: "bash_fold_flatten_stmt_list", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.repo.repo_self_build", decl_name: "default_from", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.extdeps.languages.bash_build", decl_name: "bash_build_if_else_from_stmts", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.host.fleet_keypair_mint_witness", decl_name: "refusal_poison_never_reaches_a_build_step_body", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.shell_command_text", decl_name: "shell_command_text_refusal_marker", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
